        "title": "refactor: burn down Matrix, Telegram, and outbound dead exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe unused-export ratchet stops new debt, but its grandfathered baseline still contains thousands of entries. This continuation of #106017 audits one bounded wave rather than mixing unrelated subsystems.\n\nThis PR audits all 209 baseline entries under `extensions/matrix` (47), `extensions/telegram` (99), and `src/infra/outbound` (63), then removes 75 entries still unique after rebasing: Matrix 15, Telegram 20, outbound 40. Six additional overlapping Telegram entries landed independently in #106175 during the rebase.\n\nAgainst the rebased PR base, `scripts/deadcode-exports.baseline.mjs` falls from 3,537 to 3,462 lines (-75), and required entries fall from 3,529 to 3,454.\n\nRelated: #105595 and #105575.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Checked candidates against repository references, tests, runtime/lazy-import seams, and dynamic/string-keyed access before changing visibility or deleting a re-export.\n- Preserved intentional test/runtime seams, including `testing`, `__testing`, `*ForTest`, queue storage/policy helpers, target-error helpers, and dynamically imported target resolution.\n- Left `src/plugin-sdk/` untouched; no shipped Plugin SDK contract changes.\n- Kept five directory-focused commits and refreshed the baseline after each code chunk so its diff stays mechanical.\n- Removed only dead export surface and stale imports. Excluding tests and the baseline, source is net -64 LOC (48 added, 112 deleted).\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Internal module surfaces are smaller; dead declarations and re-exports are gone; the enforced baseline is 75 entries smaller.\n\nNo changelog entry: internal dead-code cleanup only.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Remote outbound suite: 53 files, 1,065 tests passed.\n- Remote Matrix suite: 118 files, 1,463 tests passed.\n- Remote Telegram suite: 143 files, 2,727 tests passed.\n- Remote ratchet regeneration and comparison matched before the final overlap-only rebases.\n- Earlier whole-branch autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (0.97). Formatting-delta autoreview: clean (0.99).\n- Exact published-head CI is running on `b82d7d797a231668a73d6137aef491713542f7b0`; this section will be refreshed with final run IDs before merge.\n- Focused Testbox runs: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29235898276 and https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29236224423\n",
        "branch": "codex/burn-dead-exports-discord-slack",
